Yes, you can determine if a Slack message has been read or not using the Slack API. When you retrieve a message by its ID, the Slack API provides a `read` property in the message object that indicates whether the message has been read or not.

Here's an example of how to retrieve a message and check its read status using the Slack API:

```javascript
const axios = require('axios');

async function getMessage(messageId) {
  try {
    const response = await axios.get(`https://slack.com/api/messages.read`, {
      params: {
        token: 'YOUR_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN',
        channel: 'CHANNEL_ID',
        message: messageId,
      },
    });

    const message = response.data.messages[0];
    console.log(`Message ID: ${message.id}`);
    console.log(`Read status: ${message.read}`);

    return message;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
    return null;
  }
}

getMessage('YOUR_MESSAGE_ID')
  .then((message) => {
    if (message) {
      console.log(`Message read status: ${message.read}`);
    } else {
      console.log('Error fetching message.');
    }
  })
  .catch((error) => {
    console.error('Error fetching message:', error);
  });
```

Replace `YOUR_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` with your bot's token, and `CHANNEL_ID` with the channel where the message was sent.

The `read` property will be set to `true` if the message has been read, and `false` if it hasn't. Keep in mind that the read status is determined by the Slack client, so it might not be immediately updated after a message is read.

