2. Define the decorator function as follows:
```typescript
import { Injectable, CanActivate, ExecutionContext } from '@nestjs/common';

@Injectable()
export class EnvCheckDecorator implements CanActivate {
  async canActivate(context: ExecutionContext): Promise<boolean> {
    const req = context.switchToHttp().getRequest();
    const nodeEnv = req.env?.NODE_ENV;

    if (nodeEnv !== 'true') {
      return false;
    }

    return await super.canActivate(context);
  }
}
```
In this decorator, we check the `NODE_ENV` variable in the request object. If it's not set to `true`, we return `false`. Otherwise, we call the `super.canActivate()` method to continue with the middleware chain.

